# FastAPI Layered Architecture

Source: [fastapi-production-architecture](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules) — adapted for ARTSA

## Layer flow
`api/routes` → `services` → `data/repositories` → ORM / memory store

Imports flow downward only. Routers must not import SQLAlchemy or raw ORM models.

## Routers (`backend/src/api/routes/`)
- Handlers stay thin: parse input, call one service/repository method, return response
- Declare `response_model`, status codes, and tags
- WebSocket routes publish/subscribe via `telemetry_bus`; no business logic inline

## Services (`backend/src/services/`)
- Orchestrate containment evaluation, session tracking, campaign side effects
- Raise domain-specific exceptions; let middleware or route handlers map to HTTP
- No FastAPI `Request`/`Response` objects in services

## Repositories (`backend/src/data/repositories/`)
- Only layer that touches SQLAlchemy ORM or `memory_store` fallback
- `_use_memory` when `settings.is_testing` or mock session — keep test path explicit
- Map ORM ↔ Pydantic domain models in private `_to_domain` / `_to_orm` helpers

## Containment (`backend/src/containment/`)
- Detectors implement `BaseDetector.detect()`; engine coordinates scoring + verdict
- New detectors register in `ContainmentEngine.__init__`; update `CompositeScorer` flag mapping

## Do not
- Put SQL queries in route handlers
- Import `ContainmentEngine` directly from frontend-facing gateway code without going through services
- Add cross-layer circular imports
